# THE gen_c RATCHET for tests/gates/arch_boundary.zen (`make archcheck`).
#
# Every line is one direct frontend import (`path-under-src module`) that
# today's AST-driven C backend still has. docs/IR_ARCHITECTURE.md §6 migrates
# gen_c onto gen_ir construct by construct; each migrated import leaves this
# file, and ARCH_GEN_C_CEILING in the Makefile drops to the new count.
#
# THIS FILE ONLY SHRINKS. The gate refuses a line outside gen/gen_c/, a line
# whose import is gone, and a count that differs from the ceiling. Adding a
# line means a new AST/sema dependency in a backend: carry the fact in gen_ir
# instead. Generated once from the tree at 890acb1c, sorted with LC_ALL=C.
